{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789213421,"nonce":"t/taIArjHaw5v6G6l06ZhZNko5E=","title":"World handle for ash: replace process-global state, droppable interpreter, load from memory","message":"Ash has no embedding API: state lives in process-global OnceLocks\n(STD_LIBRARY, LOADED_LIBRARIES, SYMBOL_TABLE), ash_std's static GC and a\nthread-local scheduler; the interpreter is leaked at exit because brokers\nhold raw handles into its arrays; execute_entrypoint never returns when a\nmain loop is registered; functions are addressed by findex only.\n\nIntroduce caribou::World and make ash an adapter over it: per-world state,\nArc'd shared array handles so the interpreter can be dropped,\nBytecodeDecoder::from_bytes, name-keyed lookup, and a tick point inside the\nexisting frame pump so a heaps loop is unchanged. The Haxe application stays\nthe driver; caribou.Script is the driver-side API for loading spokes.","files":null}]}